  "study_summary": {
    "objective": "Test whether A. flavus and A. oryzae populations differ in transcriptomic architecture and in their response to spore density.",
    "experimental_design": "Six A. oryzae-labelled isolates, each grown on cellophane over PDA at 10^2 and 10^6 spores/ml for 100 h (one pooled sample per isolate and density; 12 libraries).",
    "main_finding": "Populations are transcriptomically differentiated and respond differently to spore density; A. oryzae shows a raised carbohydrate-metabolism module, consistent with phylogeny."
  },
